course: dictionary
lesson: 7567
title: Presence: being there, and feeling there
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Presence means being in a place, or being there. «Your presence is requested at the meeting» means please come along.
explain: «In the presence of» means with someone there. «Don't swear in the presence of children» means not while children are in the room.
explain: A presence can also be something you feel is there, even when you cannot see it. «She felt a strange presence in the room» means she sensed something there.
explain: Stage presence is a strong, confident way of standing and speaking that makes people notice you.
fact: Presence means being in a place or being there.
fact: «In the presence of» someone means with them there.
fact: In science, tests check for the presence of starch or water.
fact: «Stand up in the presence of the aged» means show respect for older people.
fact: A presence can be something you feel is there even if you cannot see it.
exercise: «She felt a strange presence in the room.» What is a presence here? | A pet cat asleep on the bed | A light switched on | *Something you can feel is there, even if you cannot see it | A loud noise from the hall
exercise: Mrs Patel writes, «Your presence is requested at the meeting.» What does she want? | Please write a letter | Please wait outside | Please leave the meeting | *Please come to the meeting
exercise: «Don't swear in the presence of children.» What does in the presence of mean? | *With them there | Instead of | Far away from | After
test: Scientists check a liquid for the presence of water. What does presence mean here? | Being taken out of the liquid | *Being there, so the water is found | Being cold | Being the right colour
test: Which phrase means a strong, confident way of standing and speaking that makes people notice you? | Stage fright | Hiding | *Stage presence | Stage lights
exam: Which meaning fits «a police presence on the street»? | Police riding bicycles | Police being sent to hospital | Police asleep in a car | *Police being there so people can see them
